# UST.G3GM Prime-Arithmetic Compatibility Correction Theorem v1

## Scope

This theorem audits the fresh-prime H02 campaign behind UST.G3GA--G3GH.  It
is a correction theorem.  It does not add a stronger name to an unchanged
packet, and it does not alter the same-field G3GK/G3GL calculation.

## Defect

The fresh-prime builder requested the primes `79903`, `81359`, and `82963`,
but imported `evaluate()` and `normalize()` from the G3DJ second-prime
runtime.  Those functions close over

```text
PRIME = 33863.
```

Thus the endpoint itself was evaluated at the requested prime while the
`Delta`, `U`, `W`, subtraction, and sparse canonicalization steps inherited
the unrelated modulus `33863`.  The resulting matrices were not finite
specializations of one common integral H02 family.

## Exact compatibility test

The defect is visible without interpretation.  Replaying the superseded
fresh-prime assembly at the archived anchor `(p,gamma)=(21817,5)` disagrees
with the archived G3DH border in the exact number of entries recorded by the
G3GM certificate.  Replacing every inherited operation by

```text
evaluate_at_prime(records, gamma, prime)
normalize_at_prime(matrix, prime)
```

reproduces the archived `30789 x 30789` border entry by entry: the sparse
difference has zero nonzero entries.

## Corrected fresh anchor

The same corrected compiler was then executed at the independent split
anchor

```text
(p,gamma) = (79903,12863).
```

Exact sparse elimination gives

```text
coupling rank    = 4748,
kernel dimension = 1274.
```

The 4,748 selected coordinates and 1,274 dependent coordinates are identical
to the archived `(21817,5)` chart.  Therefore the previously reported
`4752/1270` profile and its component-23/24 chart transition were artifacts
of mixed-modulus arithmetic.

## What survives

The corrected anchor still has the component-20 second-jet profile

```text
(15,5,0,33,17,1).
```

The canonical `210 x 132` source operator has rank 115, the same fixed row
chart completes it to an invertible `132 x 132` system, and the corrected
source replays that system exactly.  Hence the archived 48-fiber G3GG
fixed-minor formula survives and is independently confirmed at one corrected
fresh anchor.  Its promotion over `Q(gamma)` remains open.

## Corrected frontier

The accepted global interval returns to

```text
4748 <= rank_Q(gamma)(Q) <= 5102,
kernel_dimension_Q(gamma)(Q) <= 1274.
```

No equality is asserted.  The following claims are retracted pending a
prime-parameterized rebuild:

* the `4752` characteristic-zero lower bound;
* the `1270` kernel upper bound;
* the component-23/24 four-unit rank jump;
* the G3GA--G3GE mixed-prime height reconstruction.

G3GK and G3GL are unaffected because they execute at the fixed
`(21817,5)` endpoint and do not import the defective fresh-prime arithmetic.

